SURFACE PARITY — what was ported from the web source (no scope narrowing)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
• Composition : Helix badge + title + description (the verbatim PII / "never proposes or changes a
                setting" safety promise) + a right-aligned "Ask Helix" action (web buttonPlacement
                "below") + the AiOutputPanel — every region of AISafetySettingExplainer.tsx rendered
                through the AIFeatureCard scaffold, reproduced as surface-scoped private subviews
                (the atomic AIFeatureCard/AiOutputPanel/AIThinkingIndicator peers are owned by the P4
                component-library bundle — out of scope here, and not yet present natively).
• NARRATIVE   : the surface only EXPLAINS existing settings — no proposal, no "Apply to form", no
                claim of having changed a value. Streamed delta text is shown verbatim (whitespace
                preserved, text-selectable).
• Wiring rule : the action button is disabled by the COMPUTED `isBusy` (streaming || paused-confirm)
                expression (web), never a literal flag. `explain()` is a double-submit no-op while
                busy (web `handleExplain`). `stop()` cancels the in-flight stream (web cancel-on-unmount).
• withAiFeature: feature off → the WHOLE surface is withdrawn (renders nothing, ADR-015). NOT a hidden
                section: feature on + no stream → the inviting idle card renders (never a blank box).
• AiOutputPanel: every web branch reproduced — error ("Helix error: {msg}", unknown fallback) /
                streaming-no-text → AIThinkingIndicator peer / streamed-or-done text / idle → panel
                absent (web returns null). A `done`-with-empty-text is mapped to hidden so the panel
                is never a blank bordered box (the prompt's "never a blank box" rule).
• States      : gated / idle(empty) / thinking(loading) / narration(data) / error, PLUS the orthogonal
                P4 leaf connection axis live/stale/offline (freshness chip + banner; offline disables
                the action). Stale shows the chip/banner but does NOT auto-invoke the LLM — the web
                surface is explicitly opt-in, so auto-streaming would violate its safety contract
                (deliberate, documented adaptation of the sibling cards' stale auto-refresh).
• i18n        : 100% via the P1/S10 facade (SafetyExplainerStrings, table "AISafetySettingExplainer");
                zero English prose literals in Swift beyond the centralised web-default fallbacks
                (SafetyExplainerCopy). 13 keys (4 web parity + 4 scaffold + 5 P4 chrome).
• Telemetry   : P1/S11 `view.opened` emitted exactly once, deferred past the gate (web marker parity),
                slug "AISafetySettingExplainer".
• a11y        : VoiceOver labels on the action ("Ask Helix · Explain my settings", web aria-label),
                the badge, the freshness chip, the error row; header trait; Dynamic Type via Font.TS
                roles; Reduce-Motion-aware skeleton shimmer + system ProgressView.

